      ],
      "source": "https://experiencechesterfield.com/explore/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Chester County, Tennessee, was created in 1879 when Hardeman, Henderson, McNairy, and Madison counties ceded land to form the new county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sharetngov.tnsosfiles.com/tsla/history/county/factchester.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Henderson serves as the county seat of Chester County, hosting the county courthouse and administrative offices.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sharetngov.tnsosfiles.com/tsla/history/county/factchester.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1933 fire destroyed the Chester County courthouse, an event that prompted significant rebuilding efforts in the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sharetngov.tnsosfiles.com/tsla/history/county/factchester.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Bermuda Hundred, a small community in southeastern Chesterfield, holds the distinction of being America’s first incorporated town.",
